==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-tip-off.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} An obvious [[clue]] or [[indication]].
#: ''The broken window and overturned plant pots were a '''tip-off''' that something was wrong.''
# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} A [[report]] of [[suspicious]] [[behaviour]], especially to an [[authority]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=16 Aug 86|volume=14|number=5|journal=Gay Community News|page=1|author=Marcos Bisticas-Cocoves|title=Harry Hay Barred from Carrying NAMBLA Sign|text=Haws also alleged that Hay was engaged in a conspiracy to disrupt the parade. "People called a week before and said he would be doing something." The alleged '''tip-off''' was anonymous.}}
#: ''The police received a '''tip-off''' about a recent bank robbery.''

